*combine* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

Chip's build system

Bundles multiple Chippy source files into a single executable program based on the configuration in ''combine.chp''.
Programs, properly built using combine have no dependencies outside of the ''chippy'' interpreter itself.

*Usage:*
- ''chippy combine'' - Process default ''combine.chp'' configuration
- ''chippy combine path/to/config.chp'' - Process specific configuration file
- ''chippy combine new'' - Generate new template ''combine.chp'' file

*Configuration:*
- ''Project'': Output program name
- ''Version'': Program version string
- ''Licence'': Path to license file to include
- ''Output'': Output executable filename
- ''Source'': Main source file entry point
- ''Paths'': List of directories to search for dependencies
- ''External'': List of dependencies combine shouldn't bundle and just keep as loads
- ''StripComments'': Remove comments from bundled output
- ''StripWhitespace'': Remove excess whitespace from bundled output
- ''AddShebang'': Add ''#!/usr/bin/chippy'' shebang to output

*What it does:*
- Automatic dependency resolution via ''load()'' statements
- Circular dependency prevention
- Licence header insertion (when configured)
- Comment/whitespace stripping (when configured)
- Safety checks:
	- Symbol collision detection in file scope (see ''chippy doc scoping'')
	- Syntax error detection

*Returns:*
- Creates bundled executable file
- Exit code 0 on success, non-zero on failure
